The arm64 ramdisk crunches zstd into instbin and leaves out the firmware files and the Raspberry Pi's boot files.

zstd: the installer extracts the sets with zstd -dc (distrib/special/zstd, the
decompressor alone). The USB network firmware (etc/firmware) is not built yet and the
installer takes no set over the network; the Raspberry Pi's firmware, device trees and
u-boot come from packages the build does not have, and the machines EmiBSD boots on today
start through UEFI.

--- a/distrib/arm64/ramdisk/list
+++ b/distrib/arm64/ramdisk/list
@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@
 LINK	instbin					usr/bin/sed
 LINK	instbin					usr/bin/signify
 LINK	instbin					usr/bin/tee
+LINK	instbin					usr/bin/zstd
 LINK	instbin					usr/sbin/chroot
 LINK	instbin					usr/sbin/installboot
 LINK	instbin					usr/sbin/pwd_mkdb
@@ -74,60 +75,6 @@
 LINK	instbin					usr/bin/ftp-ssl usr/bin/ftp
 SPECIAL	rm usr/bin/ftp-ssl
 
